<!doctype html>
<html lang="cs">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="tactical-cz">
<title>tactical-cz · {{ title }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fafaf7;
    --paper: #f1eee6;
    --paper-soft: #f7f5ed;
    --ink: #221f1c;
    --ink-soft: #4c4842;
    --muted: #76706a;
    --rule: #d8d2c4;
    --maxw: 44rem;
    --maxw-wide: 64rem;
    --gap-1: 0.5rem;
    --gap-2: 1rem;
    --gap-3: 1.75rem;
    --gap-4: 2.75rem;
    --gap-5: 4.5rem;
    --accent: #4a7c4a;
    --accent-deep: #335633;
    --accent-soft: #e2ecdf;
    --warn: #9b5a3a;
    --warn-soft: #f4e2d4;
    --display: "Source Sans 3", -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    --mono: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
  }
  @import url("https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Sans+3:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap");

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--display); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  main, header, footer { max-width: var(--maxw); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.2rem; }
  main.wide, header.wide, .wide { max-width: var(--maxw-wide); }

  /* Header / hero */
  header { padding-top: var(--gap-4); padding-bottom: var(--gap-3); }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 2px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1; margin: 0.8rem 0 0.6rem; letter-spacing: -0.014em;
  }
  header p.lede {
    font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; max-width: 38rem;
  }
  .byline {
    margin-top: var(--gap-2); padding-top: var(--gap-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex; gap: 0.9rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .byline a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;
              border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent-soft); }
  .byline a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

  /* Pipeline strip — 3 modalities at a glance */
  .pipeline {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0.6rem; margin: var(--gap-3) 0 var(--gap-2);
  }
  .pipeline > div {
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem; background: var(--paper-soft);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 3px 3px 0;
  }
  .pipeline .ph-label {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .pipeline .ph-title { font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 2px 0; }
  .pipeline .ph-desc { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  /* Section markers */
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15;
    margin: var(--gap-4) 0 var(--gap-2); padding-top: var(--gap-2);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  h2 .section-tag {
    display: block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: var(--gap-3) 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  p, ul, ol { margin: 0 0 var(--gap-2); }
  ul, ol { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }

  /* Code */
  code, .code {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.32rem; border-radius: 2px;
  }
  pre {
    background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
    padding: var(--gap-2); border-radius: 3px;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5;
    overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  pre code { background: transparent; padding: 0; }

  /* Video */
  .video-wrap {
    margin: var(--gap-3) 0;
    background: var(--ink); border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 var(--rule);
  }
  .video-wrap video { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .video-caption {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted);
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  /* Charts */
  .chart-wrap {
    margin: var(--gap-3) 0; padding: var(--gap-2);
    background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .chart-wrap svg { display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
  .chart-caption {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  /* KPI tiles */
  .kpi-row {
    display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin: var(--gap-3) 0;
  }
  .kpi-row.c3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .kpi-row.c4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .kpi-row.c3, .kpi-row.c4 { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .pipeline { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .kpi { padding: 0.7rem 0; }
  .kpi-label {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .kpi-value {
    font-size: 1.8rem; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.05; margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .kpi-value .unit { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
  .kpi-note {
    font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 4px; line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* Tables */
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; margin: var(--gap-2) 0; }
  th, td { padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  th { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase;
       letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  tr.agree td { background: var(--accent-soft); }
  tr.disagree td { background: var(--warn-soft); }

  /* Diagnostic findings card */
  .finding {
    margin: var(--gap-3) 0; padding: var(--gap-2) var(--gap-3);
    border-radius: 3px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--paper-soft);
  }
  .finding.warn { border-left-color: var(--warn); background: #fdf6ef; }
  .finding h3 { margin-top: 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .finding p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* Minimaps grid */
  .minimap-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.2rem; margin: var(--gap-2) 0;
  }
  .minimap-cell .caption {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  details {
    margin: var(--gap-2) 0; padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    background: var(--paper-soft); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px;
  }
  details summary {
    cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft); letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  details[open] summary { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }

  footer {
    margin-top: var(--gap-5); padding: var(--gap-3) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted);
  }
  footer a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;
             border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent-soft); }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="wide">
  <span class="eyebrow">tactical-cz · phase 2 + 3 demo</span>
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ lede }}</p>

  <div class="pipeline">
    <div>
      <div class="ph-label">Phase 1 · Vision</div>
      <div class="ph-title">Roboflow sports + ByteTrack</div>
      <div class="ph-desc">Per-frame player + ball detection, tubelet tracking, pitch homography → coordinates on 120×70 m plane.</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="ph-label">Phase 2 · Events</div>
      <div class="ph-title">V-JEPA2-L + BAS head</div>
      <div class="ph-desc">Frozen video encoder + small classifier head, fine-tuned on SoccerNet BAS 2025 (4 EFL matches, 12 classes).</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="ph-label">Phase 3 · Audio</div>
      <div class="ph-title">Whisper-small (cs)</div>
      <div class="ph-desc">Czech commentary transcript, keyword-tagged into BAS classes for cross-modal validation.</div>
    </div>
    {% if agent_qa %}
    <div>
      <div class="ph-label">Phase 4 · Agent</div>
      <div class="ph-title">Claude Sonnet 4.6</div>
      <div class="ph-desc">LLM Q&amp;A over the three pipeline outputs — natural-language tactical analysis of a specific clip.</div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <!-- Pipeline grid auto-adapts to 4 columns when agent layer is present -->
  {% if agent_qa %}<style>.pipeline { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr) !important; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .pipeline { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; } }</style>{% endif %}

  <p class="byline">
    <span>{{ generated_at }}</span>
    <span><a href="{{ repo_url }}">github.com/sandovabarbora/tactical-cz</a></span>
    <span>{{ n_windows }} sliding windows · {{ device }}</span>
  </p>

  <nav style="margin-top: var(--gap-2); padding-top: var(--gap-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted); display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
    <a href="#clip" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration:none;">1 The clip</a>
    {% if tactical_summary %}<a href="#tactical" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration:none;">2 Tactical view</a>{% endif %}
    {% if commentary_summary %}<a href="#commentary" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration:none;">3 Commentary</a>{% endif %}
    {% if agent_qa %}<a href="#agent" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration:none;">4 Ask the pipeline</a>{% endif %}
    <a href="#findings" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration:none;">5 Findings</a>
    <a href="#appendix" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration:none;">6 Appendix</a>
  </nav>
</header>

<main class="wide">

<!-- ============ SHOW ============ -->

<section id="clip">
  <h2><span class="section-tag">1 · The clip</span>15 min of AC Sparta vs Viking, Conference League 2022</h2>
  <p>The {{ video_duration }}-second window is from the first half of <em>AC Sparta Praha vs Viking Stavanger</em>, UEFA Conference League qualifier, 21 July 2022. Continuous real broadcast — no cuts, no replays, no edits. The top-right panel shows the events-model's <strong>top-3 predictions</strong> for the current frame's 4-second window — <em>"MODEL SEES:"</em> framing makes clear these are predictions, not ground truth. The bottom-right chip shows overall confidence in the top-1 prediction.</p>
  <div class="video-wrap">
    <video controls preload="metadata">
      <source src="{{ annotated_video_rel }}" type="video/mp4">
    </video>
    <div class="video-caption">{{ annotated_video_rel }} · {{ video_size_mb }} MB · {{ video_duration }} s · source: {{ source_video }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if tactical_summary %}
<section id="tactical">
  <h2><span class="section-tag">2 · Vision × Events</span>Tactical view: where the action actually happens</h2>
  <p>Phase 1 vision tells you where every player is on the 120×70 m pitch. Phase 2 events tell you what's happening. Joining them on frame index gives the kind of derived signal a coach reads at a glance: action centroid, zone share, minimap snapshots at peak shots.</p>

  <div class="kpi-row c3">
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="kpi-label">Median field tilt</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ "%.0f"|format(tactical_summary.median_field_tilt_m) }}<span class="unit"> m</span></div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Action centroid on a 120 m pitch. {% if tactical_summary.median_field_tilt_m > 80 %}heavily attacking{% elif tactical_summary.median_field_tilt_m > 60 %}attacking half{% elif tactical_summary.median_field_tilt_m > 40 %}midfield{% else %}defensive half{% endif %}.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="kpi-label">Attacking-zone share</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ "%.0f"|format(tactical_summary.attacking_zone_share * 100) }}<span class="unit"> %</span></div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Of Shot+Drive top-quartile windows, the fraction in the attacking third of the pitch.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="kpi-label">Players per frame</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ "%.1f"|format(tactical_summary.n_players_per_frame_mean) }}</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Mean tracker detections. Low (≪22) = close-up camera; high = wide pitch view.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Attacking zones, per event class</h3>
  <p>For each event class, the top-quartile-confidence windows split into defensive / midfield / attacking third by action centroid. Reads "where does each kind of event happen on the pitch".</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap">{{ tactical_zone_svg | safe }}</div>

  <h3>Field tilt timeline</h3>
  <p>Mean x-position of detected players, second by second. Up = attacking surge, down = transition. Dashed lines: pitch thirds.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap">{{ tactical_tilt_svg | safe }}</div>

  {% if tactical_minimaps %}
  <h3>Minimap snapshots at peak shot moments</h3>
  <p>The {{ tactical_minimaps|length }} highest-confidence Shot windows. Green = team A (auto-clustered by kit colour on first frames), brown = team B, grey = goalkeeper or unassigned. The team labels are unsupervised K-means on HSV; no claim about Sparta-vs-opponent identification.</p>
  <div class="minimap-grid">
    {% for m in tactical_minimaps %}
    <div class="minimap-cell">
      <div class="caption">t={{ "%.1f"|format(m.second) }}s · P(Shot)={{ "%.2f"|format(m.p_shot) }} · {{ m.action_zone }} third · {{ m.n_players_visible }} players visible</div>
      {{ m.minimap_svg | safe }}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if commentary_summary %}
<section id="commentary">
  <h2><span class="section-tag">3 · Audio × Events</span>Commentary: does Czech audio agree with the video model?</h2>
  <p>Whisper-small transcribes the live Czech commentary, then a keyword dictionary tags each segment with the BAS event class it implies. For every tagged moment we look up the events-model probability at the segment midpoint frame.</p>

  <div class="kpi-row c4">
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="kpi-label">Whisper segments</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ commentary_summary.n_segments }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="kpi-label">Tagged BAS class</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ commentary_summary.n_tagged }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="kpi-label">Agree with model</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ commentary_summary.n_agree }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="kpi-label">Agreement share</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ "%.0f"|format(commentary_summary.agree_share * 100) }}<span class="unit"> %</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th class="num">Time</th>
        <th>Commentary text</th>
        <th>Tagged class</th>
        <th class="num">Model max P</th>
        <th>Model top-1</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for ev in commentary_events %}
      <tr class="{% if ev.agrees %}agree{% else %}disagree{% endif %}">
        <td class="num">{{ "%.1f"|format(ev.midpoint_s) }}s</td>
        <td><em>{{ ev.text }}</em></td>
        <td>{{ ev.bas_classes }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.2f"|format(ev.model_p_max) }}</td>
        <td>{{ ev.model_top_class }} ({{ "%.2f"|format(ev.model_top_p) }})</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--muted)">Green rows: both modalities agree (model P ≥ 0.30 on a tagged class). Warm rows: commentator said it but model didn't fire. The disagreements turn out to be the most informative signal — see the finding below.</p>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if agent_qa %}
<!-- ============ AGENT LAYER ============ -->
<section id="agent">
  <h2><span class="section-tag">4 · Ask the pipeline</span>Natural language Q&amp;A (Claude Sonnet 4.6)</h2>
  <p>The three modalities produce derived parquets — readable, but dense. The agent layer wraps them into a context window for an LLM, which then answers questions in plain language with citations back to the data. Below: five pre-computed questions in Czech and the model's answers. The agent has no access to raw video or audio, only the events / tactical / commentary summaries.</p>
  <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; margin: var(--gap-3) 0;">
  {% for qa in agent_qa %}
    <details {% if loop.index <= 2 %}open{% endif %} style="background:var(--paper-soft); border:1px solid var(--rule); padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 3px;">
      <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600; font-size:1rem; color:var(--ink); list-style:none; padding-right:1rem;">
        <span style="color:var(--accent); font-family:var(--mono); font-size:0.78rem; margin-right:0.5rem;">Q{{ loop.index }}.</span>{{ qa.question }}
      </summary>
      <div style="margin-top: 0.8rem; padding-top: 0.8rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.55;">
        {{ qa.answer_html | safe }}
      </div>
    </details>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--muted)">Cost per question: ~$0.005 (input ~3 KB pipeline context + ~600-token Czech answer). The CLI <code>uv run python -m tactical_cz.agent.qa --question "..."</code> answers any new question live; the JSON behind this section is at <code>data/processed/agent_qa_goals.json</code>.</p>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- ============ DIAGNOSTIC FINDINGS ============ -->

<section id="findings">
  <h2><span class="section-tag">5 · Findings</span>What works, what doesn't, where to look next</h2>
  <p>Two clear results from running all three layers on this clip. Each survives the smell test independently across modalities.</p>

  <div class="finding">
    <h3>★ What transfers: continuous-play patterns recognised across leagues</h3>
    <p>Training was on 4 English Football League matches (2019-2020 season). Inference is on a Conference League qualifier in 2022, different stadium (Stockholm), different broadcast crew, different kit colours, different camera operators. The model nonetheless produces a coherent timeline: Pass + Drive baseline of ~0.45 (correct — football is mostly ball-in-play with passing), Out spikes at ball-out events (max 0.86 / mean 0.12), Shot peaks at 0.72 only at specific moments. This is real cross-domain transfer from the frozen V-JEPA2 features.</p>
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      {{ shot_chart_svg | safe }}
      <div class="chart-caption">P(Shot) along the {{ video_duration }}-second match window. Sparse, well-localized spikes (mean 0.03) at the specific moments where a shot or shot-adjacent action occurs.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding warn">
    <h3>✗ Cross + Header underestimated</h3>
    <p>The model's Cross-class max P is 0.56 and Header max 0.53, but the commentary explicitly mentions crosses and headers 4-5 times in this window (around t=167s, t=357s, t=716s, t=741s). At those moments the model's top-1 prediction is usually <strong>Pass</strong> or <strong>Drive</strong> — the model sees the ball moving and infers passing, missing the specific kinematic signature of a cross or aerial duel.</p>
    <p>Cross has 486 training examples in BAS, Header 882 — that's borderline. With more training data per class (Phase 3 LoRA fine-tune or larger annotated corpus), these classes should sharpen substantially.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="finding warn">
    <h3>✗ Goal class still structurally dead (when goals do happen)</h3>
    <p>This 15-min window has no goals, so the Goal-class staying silent (max P 0.07) is correct behaviour. But the underlying limitation persists: SoccerNet BAS 2025 train split has just 16 Goal annotations across 4 matches (vs 5206 Passes, 5188 Drives). 16 examples is below the floor for the linear head to learn a distinct visual signature — on a clip that DOES contain goals (e.g. the AC Sparta goals compilation we tested before this), Goal collapses into Shot at inference time.</p>
    <p><strong>Three plausible fixes</strong> for Phase 5+: self-supervised pretraining on the 500 unannotated SoccerNet matches, class-conditional augmentation on the 16 Goal windows (temporal jitter, crop, brightness), or LoRA fine-tune the V-JEPA2 backbone on BAS so the encoder learns the "ball-crosses-line" geometry directly. The last one needs a ~$5 RunPod budget.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="finding warn">
    <h3>✗ Calibration biases on common classes</h3>
    <p>Beyond Goal, two other classes mis-behave: <strong>Out</strong> and <strong>Ball Player Block</strong> fire systematically high across all windows (mean ≈ 0.6, calibration ratio ≈ 0.9 vs 0.1 expected). This is the well-known artefact of multi-label BCE without per-class temperature scaling on imbalanced data. Per-class threshold tuning on validation (see appendix) recovers most of the signal at inference time; proper temperature scaling would fix the logits themselves.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ DATA APPENDIX ============ -->

<section id="appendix">
  <h2><span class="section-tag">6 · Appendix · Data</span>Per-class table + top-1 timeline</h2>

  <h3>Per-class calibration on this clip</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Class</th>
        <th class="num">Max P</th>
        <th class="num">Mean P</th>
        <th class="num">Mean / Max</th>
        <th class="num">Peak at</th>
        <th>Reading</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for row in per_class_table %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.cls }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(row.max_p) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(row.mean_p) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.2f"|format(row.calibration_ratio) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.1f"|format(row.at_second) }}s</td>
        <td>{% if row.calibration_ratio > 0.7 %}<span style="color:var(--warn)">over-confident</span>{% elif row.calibration_ratio < 0.3 %}localized ★{% else %}moderate{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <details>
